# NOTE: devel/, logs/, bin/, lib/, msg_gen/, srv_gen/, build_isolated/,
# devel_isolated/ were intentionally dropped from this legacy catkin-workspace
# block -- they're catkin/rosbuild workspace-output directory names, meaningless
# in this ROS2/colcon-only repo, and unanchored (no leading "/") they matched
# same-named directories anywhere in the tree -- which silently hid real
# vendored source (e.g. sbg_ros2/external/sbgECom/src/logs/, and
# unitree_lidar_sdk/lib/*.a, /bin/*) from git. See build/install/log below for
# the actual colcon-relevant ignores.
build/
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored pattern such as
# `lib/` or `bin/` matches at ANY depth, and a bare `lib/` here silently
# swallowed the prebuilt libunilidar_sdk2.a inside the vendored Unitree SDK
# when src/rover_drivers was committed, which is why unitree_lidar_sdk and
# unitree_lidar_ros2 fail to link. Do not remove the leading slashes.
/devel/
/logs/
/build/
/msg_gen/
/srv_gen/
msg/*Action.msg
msg/*ActionFeedback.msg
msg/*ActionGoal.msg
msg/*ActionResult.msg
msg/*Feedback.msg
msg/*Goal.msg
msg/*Result.msg
msg/_*.py

# Generated by dynamic reconfigure
*.cfgc
/cfg/cpp/
/cfg/*.py

# Ignore generated docs
*.dox
*.wikidoc

# eclipse stuff
.project
.cproject

# qcreator stuff
CMakeLists.txt.user

srv/_*.py
*.pcd
*.pyc
qtcreator-*
*.user

/planning/cfg
/planning/docs
/planning/src

*~

# Emacs
.#*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROS2 / colcon
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/install/
/log/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# colcon markers (COLCON_IGNORE/AMENT_IGNORE are intentional, developer-placed
# markers that disable a package from being built -- they must be tracked,
# not ignored, or a fresh clone silently loses them and colcon tries to
# build packages that were meant to be skipped)

# Vendored upstream repo kept locally for reference only, not built
# (COLCON_IGNORE'd) and not meant to be tracked -- it still carries its own
# embedded .git, so ignore it explicitly rather than leaving it untracked.
src/rover_drivers/zed2i_ws/src/zed-ros2-examples/
# unitree_lidar_sdk's CMakeLists writes executables into its own source tree
# (EXECUTABLE_OUTPUT_PATH ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/bin). Build output, not vendor
# content, so it is ignored by exact path rather than by a bare `bin/`.
src/rover_drivers/unitree_4d_lidar_l2/unilidar_sdk2-2.0.10/unitree_lidar_sdk/bin/

# colcon markers stay ignored so anyone can skip a package on their own machine.
# The four below are tracked because they fail on every machine, not just one.
COLCON_IGNORE
AMENT_IGNORE
!src/rover_drivers/unitree_4d_lidar_l2/point_lio_unilidar-2.0.2/COLCON_IGNORE
!src/rover_drivers/unitree_4d_lidar_l2/unilidar_sdk2-2.0.10/unitree_lidar_ros/COLCON_IGNORE
!src/rover_drivers/unitree_4d_lidar_l2/unilidar_sdk2-2.0.10/unitree_lidar_ros2/COLCON_IGNORE
!src/rover_drivers/unitree_4d_lidar_l2/unilidar_sdk2-2.0.10/unitree_lidar_sdk/COLCON_IGNORE

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.bag
